  "explanation": {
    "short": "The marks work differently for each class. On a low-class letter ่ gives a falling tone and ้ gives a high tone; on a high-class letter ่ gives a low tone and ้ gives a falling tone.",
    "more": "All together, with ่ and ้: mid class gives low and falling; low class gives falling and high; high class gives low and falling. The famous pair is ข่าว (news, low) and ข้าว (rice, falling). Spoken Thai really does keep them apart. High is higher than mid and often a little sharp, like a bright \"Hey!\". The word ค่ะ at the end of a woman's polite sentence is falling for this reason (low-class ค with ่), and ครับ is high, as you will see."
  },
